B.eJW=new A.y("Breathing","The trachea carries air down to your lungs. Rings of tough cartilage keep it open.")
B.f4o=new A.y("Digestion","The oesophagus squeezes food down to your stomach in waves, so you can swallow even upside down.")
B.eNZ=new A.y("Breathing","You breathe about 20,000 times a day. Spread flat, your lungs would cover a tennis court.")
B.f21=new A.y("Blood","About the size of your fist. It beats around 100,000 times a day and pumps blood round a track 100,000 km long.")
B.eRl=new A.y("Breathing","A dome-shaped muscle under your lungs. It pulls down to suck air in. A hiccup is it twitching.")
B.eV6=new A.y("Digestion","Cleans your blood and stores energy. It is the only organ that can grow back after damage.")
B.f_p=new A.y("Digestion","A small green pouch that stores bile, a juice that helps you digest fatty food.")
B.f4y=new A.y("Digestion","Acid in your stomach could dissolve metal, but a thick layer of mucus protects it.")
B.f4q=new A.y("Blood","Filters old blood cells and helps fight germs. You can live without it.")
B.f4u=new A.y("Digestion","Makes juices to digest food and insulin, a hormone that controls the sugar in your blood.")
B.eVF=new A.y("Cleaning","Clean about 180 litres of blood every day and turn the waste into urine.")
